TEST RESULT
================================================================================================
  node (pooled)  : 0.01015 vs persist 0.01011 = 1.003x  (n=3,181,619)
  combined obj   : 0.02184   (no single baseline; reported for comparability with training logs only)
  per-horizon    : h1: 0.00669/0.00666=1.004x  h2: 0.00924/0.00920=1.004x  h3: 0.01070/0.01067=1.003x  h6: 0.01304/0.01302=1.001x  h12: 0.01239/0.01233=1.005x
  by regime      : moved: 0.02027/0.02044=0.991x (n=1,573,750)  flat: 0.00024/0.00000=nanx (n=1,607,869)
  mechanisms     : ladder: 0.00810 vs persist 0.00836=0.969x vs shrink(a=0.920) 0.00815=0.994x (n=408,162)  |  ladder_moved: 0.01614 vs persist 0.01698=0.951x vs shrink(a=0.836) 0.01611=1.002x (n=200,874)  |  mece: 0.00320 vs persist 0.00484=0.662x vs shrink(a=0.566) 0.00333=0.962x (n=109,642)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HEADLINE (node): 0.991x on the 1,573,750 positions that MOVED.
  The pooled 1.003x includes 1,607,869 flat positions (51%) where persistence
  is exact by construction and no forecast can do better than tie.
  LADDER : 0.994x vs shrink(alpha=0.920) -- BEATS the shrinkage oracle.  (0.969x vs persistence, n=408,162)
  LADDER_MOVED: 1.002x vs shrink(alpha=0.836) -- does NOT beat the shrinkage oracle.  (0.951x vs persistence, n=200,874)
  MECE   : 0.962x vs shrink(alpha=0.566) -- BEATS the shrinkage oracle.  (0.662x vs persistence, n=109,642)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  MID-MOVE HEAD (B1.2), next-hour quoted mid, n=157,674 positions, k=1,657 events
    MSE 1.731e-03 | zero-move 1.706e-03 | oracle alpha*prev-hour-move 1.697e-03 (alpha=-0.081)
    vs zero-move: 1.015x  95% CI [1.003, 1.034]  (k=1,657)
    vs oracle   : 1.020x  95% CI [1.008, 1.040]  (k=1,657)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  An alpha well below 1 means the quantity genuinely mean-reverts and there
  is something for a forecaster to find; an alpha near 1 means it is a random
  walk and beating persistence on it would be surprising. That difference --
  MECE alpha ~ 0.87 against ladder alpha ~ 0.99 -- is the structural finding,
  and it follows from the constraints themselves: a MECE basket is pinned to
  a LEVEL (the legs must sum to 1), while a ladder pair is only bounded by an
  INEQUALITY (gap <= 0), which an entire half-line satisfies. There is no
  level for a ladder gap to revert to, so there is nothing to forecast.
